  "Id": 176,
  "Title": "Farewell to Prof Pauline Rea-Dickins",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "On June 11, at an event at the New Africa Hotel in Dar es Salaam, about 130 faculty, staff, students and friends of AKU, and IED, EA celebrated Professor Pauline Rea-Dickin's 5-year tenure as director of the Institute and bid her farewell. ",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClassE3DB00C225F947FC9676CADEED101EB8\">On June 11, at an event at the New Africa Hotel in Dar es Salaam, about 130 faculty, staff, students and friends of AKU, and IED, EA celebrated Professor Pauline Rea-Dickin's 5-year tenure as director of the Institute and bid her farewell. The occasion was also used to welcome the incoming director, Professor Joe Lugalla. The University was represented by Vice Provost Kweku Bentil who delivered the welcome address and read a personal message from Provost Greg Moran to Pauline and all colleagues at IED, EA.\n<div>\n   <br>\n</div><div>Along with Dr Bentil, other speakers included Assistant Professor Dr Nicholas Wachira, MEd student Natasha Kassam, IT Manager Arbogast Fabian, incoming Director Joe Lugalla, Head of Research, Professor Anjum Halai, and Pauline who delivered a short but emotional farewell speech. &#160;</div><div>\n   <br>\n</div><div>Pauline was presented with a plaque from her colleagues at AKU and she and her partner, James Dickins, were given a gift of a set of Tanzanian-made bed linens. The highlight of the evening was a 10-minute slide show, \"Down Memory Lane with Pauline,\" featuring a collection of photos of Pauline at various times at IED. The slide show and the entire programme were developed by a planning committee consisting of IED, EA faculty, staff, and student representatives, with oversight and support from the Office of the Provost.</div></div>",
